title: Aruba Central Collector Summary
agents: aruba_central_aps
catalog: hw/network/wlan
license: GPLv2
distribution: checkmk
summary: Monitors Aruba Central collection, AP counts, clients, and API rate limit.
description:
 This service is created on the Windows collector host. The agent plug-in runs
 {cencli show aps -v --json}, reads both standard output and standard error,
 locates the JSON object, and separately parses the diagnostic lines {Counts}
 and {API Rate Limit} regardless of the stream used by cencli.

 The service reports total, Up, and non-Up access points; total wireless
 clients; remaining and maximum API calls; cencli runtime; the stream carrying
 JSON; and the age of the last successful collection. A failed collection is
 {CRIT}. When a bounded last-known-good cache exists, AP piggyback data remains
 available but the collector service stays {CRIT} and reports the stale age.

 Configurable levels are available for remaining API calls, last successful
 collection age, and the number of APs not Up.
discovery:
 One service is discovered on the collector host when a valid collector JSON
 document is present in the {aruba_central_aps} agent section.
